[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
==========================================================================
ckpool has been installed.

CONFIGURATION:
  Copy the sample config and edit it:
    cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/ckpool/ckpool.conf.sample \
       %%PREFIX%%/etc/ckpool/ckpool.conf
    edit %%PREFIX%%/etc/ckpool/ckpool.conf

  Minimum required fields in ckpool.conf:
    {
      "btcd"       : [{"url":"localhost:8332","auth":"user","pass":"pass"}],
      "btcaddress" : "YOUR_BTC_ADDRESS",
      "serverurl"  : ["0.0.0.0:3333"],
      "solo"       : true
    }

  For merged mining (BTC + NMC + SYS), add:
    "aux" : [
      {"url":"localhost:8336","auth":"nmcuser","pass":"nmcpass"},
      {"url":"localhost:8370","auth":"sysuser","pass":"syspass"}
    ],
    "auxaddress" : ["YOUR_NMC_ADDRESS", "YOUR_SYS_ADDRESS"]

ENABLING THE SERVICE:
  Add to /etc/rc.conf:
    ckpool_enable="YES"

  Then start with:
    service ckpool start

NOTES:
  - bitcoind (and namecoind/syscoind for merged mining) must be running
    and fully synced before starting ckpool.
  - Logs are written to: %%PREFIX%%/var/log/ckpool/
  - The service runs as the 'ckpool' user (created automatically).
  - Stratum port default: 3333 (configure firewall accordingly).

For more information, see:
  %%PREFIX%%/share/doc/ckpool/README.md
  https://bitbucket.org/ckolivas/ckpool
==========================================================================
EOM
}
]
